# Broodspinner: Reach lets the 2/3 block Bot2's Ornithopter (0/2 flying) (CR 702.17b), which the two damage destroys. On turn 5
# the two Black Lotuses are sacrificed for mana (artifact) and the Broodspinner for its "{4}{B}{G}, {T}, Sacrifice this creature"
# ability (creature): two card types among cards in Bot1's graveyard, so two Insects and not a third (Bot2's Ornithopter, in its own
# graveyard, is not counted; the other scenario pins that with a card type only Bot2 has).

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Jet
Mox Emerald
Broodspinner
Black Lotus
Black Lotus
Swamp
Island
Island
Island
Island x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Ornithopter
Island x23

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Broodspinner.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Arrange(Island; Island |)
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T4 Bot2.DeclareAttackers]
Bot2.Attack(Ornithopter > Bot1)
Bot1.Block(Broodspinner > Ornithopter)
[T4 Bot2.Main2]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter = (absent)
? Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Green)
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Broodspinner.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Insect Token#1.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Insect Token#2.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Insect Token#3 = (absent)
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 3
